<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-expertise/">Services</a></li><li aria-current="page">Appraisal Clause Representation</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Your Appraisal Clause Appraiser in Delaware</h1><p class="lede">When the carrier accepts the loss but not the price, the appraisal provision in your policy replaces back-and-forth emails with a three-person panel. We become the appraiser you appoint.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/start-your-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Your role</dt><dd>You appoint us</dd></div><div><dt>Panel</dt><dd>2 appraisers + umpire</dd></div><div><dt>Decides</dt><dd>Amount of loss only</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>A short clause with real consequences</h2>
<p>Most homeowners, condo and commercial property forms sold in Delaware include a paragraph headed “Appraisal.” In plain terms it says: if you and the insurer can’t agree on the amount of loss, either side can demand appraisal in writing; each side picks a competent and impartial appraiser; the two appraisers pick an umpire; and a written agreement signed by any two of the three sets the amount. That signature rule is why the person you appoint matters. An appraisal clause appraiser in Delaware is not a negotiator who can be ignored — their work becomes part of a binding number.</p>
<h2>What we handle as your appointed appraiser</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Policy and demand review.</strong> We read the exact appraisal wording, any endorsements and the demand letter, and flag response windows (many forms use 20 days to name an appraiser).</li>
<li><strong>Our own inspection.</strong> We measure and photograph the property ourselves. We do not start by editing the carrier’s estimate.</li>
<li><strong>A line-item valuation.</strong> Built in industry estimating software with current pricing for your part of Delaware — a Wilmington rowhome and a Bethany Beach cottage don’t cost the same to repair.</li>
<li><strong>Working sessions with the other appraiser.</strong> Most disagreements shrink here, line by line, with photos and measurements on the table.</li>
<li><strong>Umpire selection and presentation.</strong> If items stay open, we help choose a qualified umpire and present the remaining differences clearly.</li>
<li><strong>Award review.</strong> We check that the award form separates replacement cost, actual cash value and any categories the policy treats differently before anyone signs.</li>
</ul>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Know the limits</b>Appraisal decides how much a covered loss costs. It doesn’t decide coverage, and it doesn’t award penalties or legal fees. If the carrier has denied the claim, a Delaware attorney is usually the right first call.</div>
<h2>Where appraisal tends to work</h2>
<p>The clause works best on scope and price disputes: how many roof slopes were damaged by wind off the Delaware Bay, whether hardwood can be matched after a pipe burst, what drywall and paint really cost in Kent County this season. It is a weaker tool when the real disagreement is about an exclusion, long-term wear, or whether flood water (not covered by most homeowners forms) caused the damage.</p>
<h2>Impartial, but prepared</h2>
<p>Many policies require each appraiser to be impartial. We take that seriously: we price what the evidence supports, disclose prior relationships with the other appraiser or umpire, and never take a contingency stake in the repair contract. That credibility is what moves an umpire.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can my roofer be my appraiser?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually that’s a bad idea. Policies commonly require a competent and impartial appraiser, and a contractor who stands to win the repair job may be challenged as interested, which can put the award at risk.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if the insurer is the one who demanded appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The process is the same. You still name your own appraiser within the response window the policy sets, and you are not required to use anyone the carrier suggests.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long does Delaware appraisal usually take?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Straightforward residential panels often wrap up within six to twelve weeks of both appraisers being named. Commercial losses, contents-heavy claims and umpire hearings can take longer.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="cards cards-3"><a class="card rv" href="/appraisal-expertise/homeowners-insurance-appraisal/"><span class="card-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/home-front-porch.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/home-front-porch-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/home-front-porch.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, (max-width:1100px) 50vw,